@@ -102,7 +102,7 @@ ### Ticket
 
 **Immutability enforcement:** the write-once rule is enforced on the `Ticket` model (`updating` hook), so it applies to Eloquent saves only — mass updates through the query builder (`Ticket::query()->update(...)`) bypass it and must not be used on issued tickets.
 
-**Single-ticket call (scope note):** `Ticket::call()` marks one waiting ticket as `called` (exactly-once). Deterministic call-next selection (priority + age + 3-ticket fairness) is implemented by `App\Actions\CallNextTicket` with the three call-panel modes below (`any` applies fairness; `priority_only`/`normal_only` ignore it). Both call paths enforce the **same effective queue authorization rule** (`QueuePolicy::call`): owner/admin bypass without a grant row, employees require a `queue_access.call` grant for that queue, non-members are denied with no ticket mutation. HTTP/Livewire panels remain future work.
+**Single-ticket call (scope note):** `Ticket::call()` marks one waiting ticket as `called` (exactly-once). Deterministic call-next selection (priority + age + 3-ticket fairness) is implemented by `App\Actions\CallNextTicket` with the three call-panel modes below (`any` applies fairness; `priority_only`/`normal_only` ignore it). Both call paths enforce the **same effective queue authorization rule** (`QueuePolicy::call`): owner/admin bypass without a grant row, employees require a `queue_access.call` grant for that queue, non-members are denied with no ticket mutation. The attendant panel (`App\Livewire\Entity\Serve`) resolves the selected queue scoped to the entity, lists only queues the user may call (active; all for owner/admin, granted ones for employees), surfaces `InactiveQueueException`/`NoWaitingTicketsException` as notices, lets `AuthorizationException` through as 403, and rate-limits successful calls to 10/min per user and entity. Queue management (`App\Livewire\Entity\Queues`, owner/admin) calls the same actions; renaming re-derives the slug from the new name and every client-supplied queue/membership id is resolved through `$entity->queues()` / `$entity->memberships()`.
 
